{"name":"Whirlwind","hex":"#e2d5d3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whirlwind","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A windstorm of limited extent, such as a tornado, dust devil, or waterspout, characterized by an inward spiral motion of the air with an upward current in the center; a vortex of air.","A person or body of objects or events sweeping violently onward."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Rapid and minimal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whirlwind"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whirlwind","blocks":[{"text":"A whirlwind is a phenomenon in which a vortex of wind forms due to instabilities and turbulence created by heating and flow (current) gradients. Whirlwinds can vary in size and last from a few minutes to a few hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Whirlwind-001.jpg/330px-Whirlwind-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whirlwind"},{"title":"Whirlwind (Lainey Wilson album)","blocks":[{"text":"Whirlwind is the fifth studio album by American country singer Lainey Wilson. It was released on August 23, 2024, by BBR Music Group. The album was promoted by three singles \"Hang Tight Honey\", \"4x4xU\" and \"Somewhere Over Laredo\". A deluxe re-issue of the album was released on August 22, 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d9/Lainey_Wilson_-_Whirlwind.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whirlwind_(Lainey_Wilson_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Whirlwind_example.jpg/330px-Whirlwind_example.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Whirlwind_example.jpg/330px-Whirlwind_example.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu